<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
	Deliberately NOT sandboxed, and this is a decision rather than an omission.

	The sandbox redirects HOME into ~/Library/Containers/<bundle id>/Data, which
	moves settings, presets, skins and delivery targets somewhere most people do
	not know exists. Bel's configuration is designed to be edited by hand, mailed
	to somebody and kept in version control — see the Configuration section of
	README.md — and a container defeats all three. It also stops BEL_CONFIG_DIR
	from pointing anywhere outside itself, and the denial surfaces as "could not
	read <file>", which reads like a corrupt file rather than a permission.

	The cost is Mac App Store eligibility, which Bel does not want: docs/PLAN.md
	ships dmg, msix, AppImage and flatpak. Notarisation and the hardened runtime,
	which dmg distribution does need, do not require the sandbox.

	The entitlements below are kept because they are correct declarations of what
	Bel does, and because they are what the sandbox would need if it ever comes
	back. Do not re-add app-sandbox without moving the configuration story with
	it.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
